,"self_n":0,"hn_score":2.0,"first":1636761906,"last":1636761906,"show_hn":null,"n_lab":1,"pos_pct":0,"neg_pct":0,"mood":null,"quotes":[{"id":29206011,"k":"ios:1547912640","type":"comment","by":"gxnxcxcx","time":1636761906,"text":"uBlacklist fully supports blocking results from Google, Bing and DDG, and partially from Startpage and Ecosia [1]. It's been available for Firefox and Chromium derivatives for a while, and there seems to be a third-party Safari port as well [2][3].\n\nThere's a bunch of language-specific blocklists on GitHub focused on StackOverflow/GitHub mirrors and wonky machine translations, but I don't know of any mature curation effort yet.\n\n[1] https://github.com/iorate/uBlacklist#supported-search-engines\n\n[2] https://github.com/HoneyLuka/uBlacklist/tree/safari-port/safari-project\n\n[3] https://apps.apple.com/us/app/ublacklist-for-safari/id1547912640?mt=12","title":null,"story_id":29198575,"story_title":"Searx – Privacy-respecting metasearch engine","story_score":299,"comments":0,"w":1.0,"u":0,"s":"neu","self":false}],"slug":"ublacklist-for-safari"}